{"sections":[{"type":"Header","title":"Employment, unemployment and economic inactivity in Craven","label":"How Craven compares with Yorkshire and The Humber and Great Britain across employment-related statistics"},{"id":"mainlines","type":"Summary","title":"in Craven:","content":"<a name=\"section-top\"></a>","sections":[{"indicator":"Employment rate","value":"75.1%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Employment in Craven has increased compared with the previous year</p><p><a href=\"#section-employment\">Go to employment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Unemployment rate","content":"<p>Unemployment in Yorkshire and The Humber (Data are unavailable for Craven) </p><p><a href=\"#section-unemployment\">Go to unemployment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Claimant Count","value":"1.6%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Claimant Count was around the same in the year ending July 2023 than a year earlier. Claimant Count measures the number of people who are <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/aguidetolabourmarketstatistics#claimant-count\">claiming unemployment-related benefits.</a>  </p><p><a href=\"#section-claimant\">Go to Claimant Count section</a>  </p>"},{"indicator":"Economic inactivity","value":"1.6%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Economic inactivity has increased since the previous year. These are people who are neither employed nor seeking work.</p><p><a href=\"#section-inactive\">Go to economic inactivity section</a></p>"}]},{"type":"Caveat","content":"<p>All estimates are based on the <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/surveys/informationforhouseholdsandindividuals/householdandindividualsurveys/labourforcesurvey\"> Labour Force Survey</a>. Data for local areas are based on smaller sample sizes than national figures and may vary more year to year.</p>"},{"type":"Employment_rate","content":"<a name=\"section-employment\"></a><h2>Employment in Craven has increased compared with the previous year</h2><p>Craven's employment rate was higher than across Yorkshire and The Humber as a whole in the year ending March 2023.</p><p>Of people aged 16 to 64 years living in Craven, 75.1% were employed in the year ending March 2023. This is an increase compared with the year ending March 2022 when the local rate was 75.0%.</p><p>Across Yorkshire and The Humber in the year ending  March 2023, 74.4% of people aged 16 to 64 years were employed. This was higher compared with the previous year, when 74.3% of people were employed.</p>"},{"id":"chart-timeseries","type":"Chart","chartType":"line-highlight","title":"Employment rate in Yorkshire and The Humber among those aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending 2012 to year ending March 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"z":"York","x":"2012","y":75.5},{"z":"York","x":"2013","y":74.9},{"z":"York","x":"2014","y":73.2},{"z":"York","x":"2015","y":74.1},{"z":"York","x":"2016","y":76.1},{"z":"York","x":"2017","y":77.6},{"z":"York","x":"2018","y":77},{"z":"York","x":"2019","y":78.4},{"z":"York","x":"2020","y":80},{"z":"York","x":"2021","y":76.7},{"z":"York","x":"2022","y":81.8},{"z":"York","x":"2023","y":83.6},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2012","y":63.9},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2013","y":69},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2014","y":68.7},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2015","y":70.6},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2016","y":68.4},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2017","y":69},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2018","y":70.4},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2019","y":74.6},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2020","y":73.1},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2021","y":69.5},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2022","y":75.8},{"z":"Sheffield","x":"2023","y":71.8},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2012","y":67.4},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2013","y":68.8},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2014","y":69},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2015","y":70.1},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2016","y":74.2},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2017","y":74.9},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2018","y":76.9},{"z":"Leeds","x":"2019","y":75.5},{"z":"Leeds","x"