d 16 to 64 years were economically inactive, compared with 21.5% in the same period of March 2022.</p>"},{"id":"chart-inactivity","type":"Chart","chartType":"bar","title":"Highest economic inactivity rates in Yorkshire and The Humber, residents aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending March 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"x":25.9,"y":"North East Lincolnshire"},{"x":25.8,"y":"Rotherham"},{"x":25.7,"y":"Kirklees"},{"x":25.6,"y":"Bradford"},{"x":25.4,"y":"Barnsley"}],"padding-left":"160"},{"type":"end","content":"<p><a href=\"#section-top\">Back to top</a></p>"},{"type":"Nomis","content":"<h2>More data on the Craven labour market </h2><p>You can view and download more data on the labour market on the <a href=\"https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/reports/lmp/la/1946157113/report.aspx\">Craven area profile page on Nomis.</a>  </p>"},{"type":"About","content":"<h2>About the data</h2><p>The content in this article is generated using semi-automated journalism, based on rules pre-programmed by Office for National Statistics (ONS) staff.</p><p>This is a new product in Beta release, intended to improve the accessibility of labour market data to local authority level. Leave us feedback. </p>"}],"place":{"areacd":"E07000163","areanm":"Craven","geography":"Non-metropolitan District","parentcd":"E12000003","parentnm":"Yorkshire and The Humber","total_authorities":21,"supergroupnm":"Countryside Living","groupnm":"English and Welsh Countryside","subgroupnm":"Older Farming Communities","total_supergroup_national":70,"total_supergroup_regional":7,"total_group_national":42,"total_group_regional":6,"total_subgroup_national":19,"total_subgroup_regional":3,"county_combinedcd":"E06000065","county_combinednm":"North Yorkshire","nomis_code":1946157113,"nomis_url":"https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/reports/lmp/la/1946157113/report.aspx","claimant_count_jul_2012":241.67,"claimant_count_jul_2013":177.5,"claimant_count_jul_2014":111.67,"claimant_co